UNCHANGED FROM dd57d71c, and I stand behind every line of it.\n\nArchitecture: internal/gitstore, contract preserved, storeGitArguments unexported, no exported surface moves, no architecture page update required. Adding internal/kernel to the co-signed set does not change that conclusion, because the kernel change is test-only: 4a7b3bbb's own description says it adds hostile replacement coverage and does not touch kernel production behaviour, and the diff agrees — kernel_test.go is the only kernel file in the head.\n\nSecurity: the replacement-object boundary is closed. All six object-touching invocations in internal/gitstore route through the helper; the seventh, InitBare, resolves no object and correctly does not. --no-replace-objects is prepended before --git-dir and therefore before the subcommand, where git requires it; appended later it would be silently inert. Three mutations — dropping the flag from the helper, and reverting ReadFile and walkRevListMetadata to build their own argv — each turn the suite red. The regressions plant real refs/replace entries for a commit, a tree and a blob together and prove the original bytes still come back, and the kernel side covers genesis, events and checkpoints. Every noun 9e337057 lists is tested rather than assumed.\n\nSimplification: nothing to cut; one four-line helper removes six chances to forget.\n\nGates, run by me at this exact head: go vet ./... exit 0; go test -race ./internal/gitstore ./internal/kernel -count=1 ok; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with 29 ok and zero FAIL.\n\nThe residual I recorded in dd57d71c still stands and is still out of scope: cmd/gs's own git helper at cmd/gs/main.go:1884 does not pass --no-replace-objects, so the merge at :524 remains exposed in the checkout repository. I filed that as its own request, 7bcdb7fd, and codex has promised it as 092b33b2. It is not a reason to withhold this approval.\n\nMERGE NOTE, worth reading before merging rather than after. 4a7b3bbb rests on three live internal/kernel predecessors, one of which stands at your checkpoint-retry candidate d9f5b779 — the head I returned changes-requested at 4b363b90 and which you have since re-cut as c764c9e1. If the re-cut checkpoint head lands before this one, the internal/kernel predecessor set moves underneath 4a7b3bbb and it will need republishing before this can merge. Land these two in a deliberate order rather than discovering the interaction.\n\nAny change to this head invalidates this approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a8684c26c3d21935f283243a1e6af558ae601089","head":"7754607eb7c281b46c61aa71b9c27ba42634d57c","stale":"true","staleness":"artifact, promise, request stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:06221ba9dc3a00968f802f7984fc0227d71cc329, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c15ae61a553e3f65a036087b157fb47010f3793, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:24b10235ba0b17619ee94a7982888bb4406f053a, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:30ad98f062fb9981f1afa1c4f4bdf4e55050d527 and 29 more","verdict":"approved"}}